            answer: `<h3>What Is the Tab Key?</h3>
  <p>The <strong>Tab key</strong> is a special key on a computer keyboard. It is used to move the cursor forward by a set amount of space or to move between different fields in a form.</p>

  <h4>Where Is the Tab Key Located?</h4>
  <p>The Tab key is usually located on the left side of the keyboard, above the Caps Lock key and to the left of the Q key.</p>

  <h4>Uses of the Tab Key</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Creating space:</strong> It moves the cursor forward, often creating an indent or a wider gap in text.</li>
    <li><strong>Moving between form fields:</strong> It helps move from one box to another, such as from the Name field to the Email field.</li>
    <li><strong>Organizing text:</strong> It can help align text or information in documents.</li>
    <li><strong>Moving between options:</strong> In many applications, it moves the selection to the next button or control.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>How to Use the Tab Key</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Place the cursor where you want to move forward.</li>
    <li>Press the Tab key once.</li>
    <li>The cursor will move to the next tab position or field, depending on the program you are using.</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>Examples of the Tab Key</h4>
  <table>
    <tr><td><strong>Where You Use It</strong></td><td><strong>What Happens</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><td>In a text document</td><td>Moves the cursor forward and may create an indent.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>In an online form</td><td>Moves from one field to the next.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>On a website</td><td>Moves focus to the next interactive item, such as a link or button.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>In a list</td><td>Can help indent text or organize information in supported programs.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h4>Tab Key and Spacebar: Difference</h4>
  <table>
    <tr><td><strong>Tab Key</strong></td><td><strong>Spacebar</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Moves the cursor to a tab position or the next field.</td><td>Inserts a space between words.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Often creates a wider gap or an indent.</td><td>Usually creates one space at a time.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h4>Remember</h4>
  <p>The Tab key helps us organize text and move quickly between fields and options. Its exact action depends on the program being used.</p>`,
