            answer: `<h3>What Is Left Click?</h3>
  <p>A <strong>left click</strong> is one of the most common actions performed using a computer mouse. It means pressing and releasing the left button of the mouse one time.</p>
  <p>We use left-clicking to select items, open buttons, place the cursor, and perform different tasks on a computer.</p>

  <h4>Uses of Left Click</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Select an item:</strong> Click on a file or folder to select it.</li>
    <li><strong>Open a button:</strong> Click a button on a website or application.</li>
    <li><strong>Place the cursor:</strong> Click inside a text box to start typing.</li>
    <li><strong>Select text:</strong> Click and drag the mouse to select words or sentences.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose an option:</strong> Click an option in a menu.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>How to Perform a Left Click</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Move the mouse pointer to the item you want to select.</li>
    <li>Press the left mouse button once.</li>
    <li>Release the button.</li>
    <li>The item will usually be selected or the chosen action will be performed.</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>Important Point</h4>
  <p>A <strong>single left click</strong> usually selects an item, while a <strong>double-click</strong> is commonly used to open a file or folder on the desktop.</p>`,
