            answer: `<h3>What Is Right Click?</h3>
  <p>A <strong>right click</strong> is an action performed using the right button of a computer mouse. We press and release the right mouse button once to perform a right click.</p>
  <p>Right-clicking usually opens a <strong>context menu</strong>. This menu shows different options related to the item we clicked on.</p>

  <h4>Uses of Right Click</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Open a context menu:</strong> View options related to an item.</li>
    <li><strong>Copy a file:</strong> Right-click a file and choose the Copy option.</li>
    <li><strong>Rename a file:</strong> Right-click a file and choose Rename.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete a file:</strong> Right-click a file and choose Delete.</li>
    <li><strong>View webpage options:</strong> Right-click a webpage to see available options.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>How to Perform a Right Click</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Move the mouse pointer to the file, folder, or item you want to use.</li>
    <li>Press the right mouse button once.</li>
    <li>A context menu will usually appear on the screen.</li>
    <li>Click the option you want to choose.</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>Difference Between Left Click and Right Click</h4>
  <table>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Left Click</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Right Click</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Usually selects an item or performs an action.</td>
      <td>Usually opens a menu of additional options.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Example: Select a folder.</td>
      <td>Example: Open the folder's options menu.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h4>Important Point</h4>
  <p>The options shown after a right click depend on the item, application, and operating system you are using.</p>`,
