            answer: `<h3>What Is a Window?</h3>
  A window is a rectangular area on the computer screen where an application, file, or folder is displayed. When we open an application such as Paint, Calculator, or File Explorer, it usually appears inside a window.

  <h4>Main Parts of a Window</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Title Bar:</strong> Shows the name of the application, file, or document.</li>
    <li><strong>Minimize Button:</strong> Hides the window from the main screen and keeps the application available on the taskbar.</li>
    <li><strong>Maximize Button:</strong> Makes the window fill the screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Restore Button:</strong> Changes a maximized window back to its previous size.</li>
    <li><strong>Close Button:</strong> Closes the window.</li>
    <li><strong>Scroll Bar:</strong> Helps us move up, down, left, or right to view content that is not fully visible.</li>
    <li><strong>Menu or Toolbar:</strong> Provides commands and tools for working in an application, depending on the program.</li>
    <li><strong>Window Border:</strong> The edge of a window that may be used to change its size.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Uses of a Window</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>To view and use an application.</li>
    <li>To open and work with files and folders.</li>
    <li>To read, write, draw, or calculate.</li>
    <li>To move between different open applications.</li>
    <li>To resize, minimize, maximize, or close an application.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>How to Manage a Window</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Open an application, such as Calculator.</li>
    <li>Click the Minimize button to hide its window temporarily.</li>
    <li>Click the application icon on the taskbar to return to it.</li>
    <li>Click the Maximize button to make the window fill the screen.</li>
    <li>Click the Close button when you have finished using the application.</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>Important Point</h4>
  We can often keep multiple application windows open at the same time and switch between them to do different tasks.`,
