            answer: `<h3>What Is Restore?</h3>
  Restore, also called Restore Down, is an option that changes a maximized window back to its previous, smaller size. It allows us to see the desktop or other open windows around the application.

  <h4>Restore Button</h4>
  In Windows, the Restore Down button usually appears in the upper-right corner of a maximized window. It often looks like two overlapping squares. When we click it, the window returns to a smaller size instead of filling the entire screen.

  <h4>Uses of Restore</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>To change a maximized window back to a smaller size.</li>
    <li>To see other open windows on the desktop.</li>
    <li>To work with two application windows more easily.</li>
    <li>To make it easier to move or resize a window.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>How to Restore a Window</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Open an application, such as Paint or a web browser.</li>
    <li>Click the Maximize button to make the window fill the screen.</li>
    <li>Find the Restore Down button in the upper-right corner.</li>
    <li>Click the Restore Down button.</li>
    <li>The window returns to its previous, smaller size.</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>Remember the Difference</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Minimize:</strong> Hides the window from the desktop while usually keeping the application open.</li>
    <li><strong>Maximize:</strong> Makes the window fill the screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Restore:</strong> Changes a maximized window back to its previous size.</li>
    <li><strong>Close:</strong> Closes the application window.</li>
  </ul>`,
