            answer: `<h3>What Is a Search Engine?</h3>
  A <strong>search engine</strong> is an online tool that helps us find information on the Internet. We can use it to search for answers, pictures, videos, websites, news, and many other things.

  <h4>How Does a Search Engine Work?</h4>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open a search engine:</strong> Open a search engine in your web browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Type a search query:</strong> Enter the words or questions about what you want to find.</li>
    <li><strong>View the results:</strong> The search engine shows a list of websites, images, videos, and other useful information.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose a result:</strong> Click a suitable result to learn more about your topic.</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>Examples of Search Engines</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google:</strong> Helps us find websites, images, videos, maps, and answers.</li>
    <li><strong>Bing:</strong> A search engine developed by Microsoft.</li>
    <li><strong>Yahoo Search:</strong> Helps users find information on the Internet.</li>
    <li><strong>DuckDuckGo:</strong> A search engine known for its focus on user privacy.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Search Engine vs. Web Browser</h4>
  A <strong>web browser</strong> is a program used to open websites, while a <strong>search engine</strong> is a tool used to find information online. For example, Google Chrome is a web browser, and Google Search is a search engine.

  <h4>Important Safety Tips</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Use clear words to find the information you need.</li>
    <li>Check information on reliable websites.</li>
    <li>Do not click suspicious links or unknown advertisements.</li>
    <li>Never share your password, home address, or other personal information online.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Why Are Search Engines Useful?</h4>
  Search engines help students learn new things, complete homework, find educational videos, discover pictures, and quickly get information about different subjects.`,
