            question: "Mobile-First Design",
            answer: "Mobile-first design means creating the basic layout for small screens first and then adding styles for larger screens. It encourages simple layouts and helps prioritize important content.",
            example: "/* Base styles for mobile */\n.container {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  gap: 16px;\n}\n\n/* Add columns on larger screens */\n@media (min-width: 768px) {\n  .container {\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);\n  }\n}",
