            question: "Flexible Widths and Heights",
            answer: "Flexible dimensions let elements adapt to the space available. Percentage widths, max-width, min-height, and CSS layout systems help prevent content from overflowing or becoming too small.",
            example: ".container {\n  width: 90%;\n  max-width: 1100px;\n  margin-inline: auto;\n}\n\n.card {\n  min-height: 180px;\n  height: auto;\n}",
