            id: 7,
            question: "Relative Units: %, em and rem",
            answer: "Relative CSS units help create flexible designs. The % unit is relative to a relevant containing dimension or property context. The em unit depends on the element's font size in most sizing contexts, while rem depends on the root element's font size.",
            example: "html {\n  font-size: 16px;\n}\n\n.container {\n  width: 90%;\n}\n\n.card {\n  padding: 1em;\n  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n}",
