            id: 9,
            question: "Microtasks and Macrotasks",
            answer: "Microtasks include promise reactions and callbacks scheduled with queueMicrotask(). Tasks, often called macrotasks, include callbacks from setTimeout() and many event handlers. After the current synchronous code finishes, the runtime generally drains the microtask queue before moving to the next task.",
            example: "console.log(\"Start\");\n\nsetTimeout(() => {\n  console.log(\"Timer task\");\n}, 0);\n\nPromise.resolve().then(() => {\n  console.log(\"Promise microtask\");\n});\n\nconsole.log(\"End\");\n\n// Output:\n// Start\n// End\n// Promise microtask\n// Timer task",
