            id: 19,
            question: "Web APIs",
            answer: "Web APIs are browser-provided interfaces that let JavaScript interact with browser features and web resources. Examples include the DOM, Fetch API, timers, localStorage, and geolocation. They are provided by the browser environment rather than being all part of the core JavaScript language.",
            example: "// DOM API\nconst heading = document.querySelector(\"h1\");\n\n// Timer API\nsetTimeout(() => {\n  console.log(\"Timer finished\");\n}, 1000);\n\n// Fetch API\nfetch(\"https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/todos/1\")\n  .then(response => response.json())\n  .then(data => console.log(data))\n  .catch(error => console.error(error));",
