            id: 16,
            question: "Context API",
            answer: "React Context lets components share values across a component tree without passing props through every intermediate component. It is useful for values such as the current theme, language, or authenticated user. Frequently changing or complex state may need a different state-management approach.",
            example: "import { createContext, useContext } from \"react\";\n\nconst ThemeContext = createContext(\"light\");\n\nfunction ThemeLabel() {\n  const theme = useContext(ThemeContext);\n  return <p>Current theme: {theme}</p>;\n}\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <ThemeContext.Provider value=\"dark\">\n      <ThemeLabel />\n    </ThemeContext.Provider>\n  );\n}",
            image: "",
