            id: 10,
            question: "What Is JSON?",
            answer: "JSON stands for JavaScript Object Notation. It is a text-based data format used to exchange structured information between applications. JSON supports objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, and null.",
            example: "const user = {\n  \"name\": \"Ali\",\n  \"age\": 25,\n  \"isActive\": true\n};\n\nconst jsonText = JSON.stringify(user);\nconst parsedUser = JSON.parse(jsonText);",
