            question: "What Is Mongoose?",
            answer: "Mongoose is an object data modeling library for Node.js and MongoDB. It provides schemas, models, validation, middleware, and convenient methods for querying and updating documents.",
            example: "const mongoose = require('mongoose');\n\nmongoose.connect(process.env.MONGODB_URI)\n  .then(() => console.log('MongoDB connected'))\n  .catch((error) => console.error('Connection failed:', error.message));\n\nThis connects a Node.js application to MongoDB using a connection string stored in an environment variable.",
