            question: "Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)",
            answer: "Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) is a vulnerability in which an attacker causes malicious script to execute in another user's browser. It can occur when untrusted content is inserted into a page unsafely. Prevention includes context-aware output encoding, safe DOM APIs, careful HTML sanitization, and a suitable Content Security Policy.",
            example: "Avoid inserting untrusted content with element.innerHTML. Prefer element.textContent = userInput when displaying plain text. If HTML must be allowed, use a well-maintained HTML sanitizer and apply appropriate security controls.",
