              "Mocking replaces a real dependency with a controlled fake or simulated version so a test can focus on the behavior being checked. Test fixtures are reusable setup data or resources used to prepare a consistent testing environment.",
            example:
              "import { expect, test, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\nconst sendEmail = vi.fn();\n\nsendEmail(\"user@example.com\");\n\nexpect(sendEmail).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\"user@example.com\");\n\n// A fixture could be a reusable test user:\nconst testUser = {\n  id: \"user-1\",\n  name: \"Ali\",\n  email: \"ali@example.com\"\n};",
