            question: "Introduction to Rust",
            answer: "Rust is a modern systems programming language focused on performance, memory safety, and concurrency. It helps developers build reliable applications without requiring a garbage collector. Rust is commonly used for command-line tools, system software, WebAssembly, and backend services.",
