            question: "Variables and Mutability",
            answer: "In Rust, variables are immutable by default, which means their values cannot be changed after assignment. Use the mut keyword when a variable needs to change. The let keyword declares variables, while const declares compile-time constants with an explicit type.",
            example: "fn main() {\n    let name = \"Abubakar\";\n    let mut age = 25;\n    age = 26;\n\n    const MAX_SCORE: u32 = 100;\n\n    println!(\"Name: {name}\");\n    println!(\"Age: {age}\");\n    println!(\"Maximum score: {MAX_SCORE}\");\n}",
            image: "",
