            id: 4,
            question: "Conditions and Loops",
            answer: "Rust uses if and else for conditional decisions. It provides loop for repeating indefinitely, while for condition-based repetition, and for for iterating over collections or ranges. A loop can return a value using break with a value.",
            example: "fn main() {\n    let marks = 85;\n\n    if marks >= 40 {\n        println!(\"Pass\");\n    } else {\n        println!(\"Fail\");\n    }\n\n    for i in 1..=5 {\n        println!(\"{i}\");\n    }\n\n    let mut count = 3;\n    while count > 0 {\n        println!(\"Count: {count}\");\n        count -= 1;\n    }\n\n    let result = loop {\n        break 100;\n    };\n    println!(\"Result: {result}\");\n}",
