            question: "Variables and Data Types",
            answer: "Kotlin uses val to declare read-only variables and var to declare variables that can be reassigned. Common data types include Int, Double, Float, Boolean, Char, and String. Kotlin can often determine a variable's type automatically.",
            example: "fun main() {\n    val name: String = \"Abubakar\"\n    var age: Int = 25\n    val height = 1.75\n    val isDeveloper = true\n    val grade = 'A'\n\n    age = 26\n\n    println(\"Name: $name\")\n    println(\"Age: $age\")\n    println(\"Height: $height\")\n    println(\"Developer: $isDeveloper\")\n    println(\"Grade: $grade\")\n}",
