            id: 3,
            question: "Null Safety",
            answer: "Kotlin's null safety system helps prevent errors caused by accessing missing values. A variable declared with a type such as String cannot normally hold null, while String? can. Operators such as ?. safely access properties, ?: provide a fallback value, and !! forces a non-null assumption but may throw an exception.",
            example: "fun main() {\n    var name: String? = \"Sara\"\n\n    println(name?.length)\n\n    name = null\n    println(name?.length) // Prints null\n\n    val displayName = name ?: \"Guest\"\n    println(displayName)\n}",
            image: "",
