            id: 2,
            question: "Constants and Variables",
            answer: "Swift uses let to declare constants and var to declare variables. A constant cannot be reassigned after its initial value is set, while a variable can change. Swift can often determine the data type automatically.",
            example: "let name = \"Abubakar\"\nvar age = 25\nlet language = \"Swift\"\n\nage = 26\n\nprint(\"Name: \\(name)\")\nprint(\"Age: \\(age)\")\nprint(\"Language: \\(language)\")",
