            question: "SwiftUI Basics",
            answer: "SwiftUI is Apple's declarative framework for building user interfaces across Apple platforms. Developers describe how the interface should look based on state, and SwiftUI updates the view when that state changes. Common components include Text, Button, VStack, HStack, and @State.",
