            question: "Coding and Implementation",
            answer: "Coding and implementation is the phase in which developers turn the software design into working code. They create frontend interfaces, backend services, database operations, and integrations. Developers commonly use version control, coding standards, code reviews, and automated checks to keep the code organized and reliable.",
            example: "Developers build a teacher login page, create an API for recording attendance, connect the API to the database, and display attendance records on the dashboard. Git and GitHub can be used to track changes and collaborate with other developers.",
            image: "",
            video: "",
            example_image: ""
