            id: 4,
            question: "Monolithic Architecture",
            answer: "Monolithic architecture organizes an application as a single deployable unit. Features such as authentication, product management, and payments may be separated into modules, but they are typically built and deployed together. This architecture can be simple to develop and operate initially, although scaling or changing individual parts independently can be difficult.",
            example: "An online store built with one Node.js application may contain login, product listing, cart, order processing, and payment modules that are deployed together.",
            image: "",
            video: "",
            example_image: ""
