            id: 2,
            question: "What Is the Difference Between PWAs and Native Apps?",
            answer: "A PWA is delivered primarily through web technologies and runs through a browser or supported installed web-app environment. A native app is built for a particular platform or through a native development framework and can access platform features through its APIs and permissions. PWAs can simplify deployment, while native apps may provide deeper integration or capabilities that are unavailable to a PWA on a particular platform.",
