            question: "What Is Offline-First App Design?",
            answer: "Offline-first design allows an application to provide important functionality even when the internet is unavailable. The app stores suitable data locally, reads from local storage when possible, and queues changes that need to be synchronized. Developers must plan for conflicting edits, failed synchronization, stale information, and clear feedback about whether changes have reached the server.",
            example: "A field worker records an inspection without internet access. The app saves the inspection locally and uploads it when connectivity returns.",
