            question: "What Is Data Synchronization?",
            answer: "Data synchronization keeps information consistent between different copies of data, such as a local database and a cloud server. A synchronization process may upload local changes, download remote updates, retry failed operations, and resolve conflicts. Applications should use reliable identifiers and track synchronization status so that retries do not accidentally create duplicate records.",
