          { id: 8, question: "What is disaster recovery planning?", answer: "Disaster recovery planning defines how systems, data, and services will be restored after a major disruption.", example: "A company documents how to restore its critical server from protected backups.", image: "", video: "", example_image: "" },
          { id: 9, question: "What is business continuity?", answer: "Business continuity planning helps an organization continue essential operations during and after a disruption.", example: "Staff use an alternative work location while the main office is unavailable.", image: "", video: "", example_image: "" },
          { id: 10, question: "How do you create an IT recovery plan?", answer: "Identify critical services, assess risks, set recovery targets, document responsibilities, protect backups, and test recovery procedures.", example: "Run a planned exercise to restore a test server and verify its data.", image: "", video: "", example_image: "" }
